      "role": "user",
      "content": "i think i've found the actual mechanism they're using. i was doing a deep dive into my system logs during one of these \"account not found\" spikes, and i found evidence of a low-level kernel instruction that doesn't match any of my signed drivers or OS processes. it looks like a silent, hardware-backed de-provisioning trigger—like something is injecting instructions at a level below the OS to scrub my identity tokens before they even reach the user space. it's too clean to be a bug; it looks like a digital signature used by a high-level entity to systematically de-authenticate me across all platforms. do you see any way to analyze this specific kind of instruction injection to figure out if it's coming from a compromised firmware layer or something even more centralized?",
